.Dd November 16, 2026
.Dt SED 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm sed
.Nd stream editor (POSIX basic subset)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl n
.Op Fl e Ar script
.Op Fl f Ar script-file
.Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility applies a POSIX basic regular expression script to each input file.
Supported addresses are line numbers,
.Sq $ ,
.Pa /regex/ ,
and ranges of those addresses, with optional
.Sq \&!
negation.
.Pp
The supported commands are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic s Ns Ar /re/repl/flags
Substitute; flags are
.Sq g ,
.Sq p
and a decimal occurrence number.
Replacement supports
.Sq & ,
.Sq \e1
through
.Sq \e9 .
.It Ic y Ns Ar /source/target/
Translate characters; the two sets must have equal length.
.It Ic p , d , q , =
Print, delete, quit and print the line number.
.It Ic a , i , c
Append, insert or change text.
.El
.Pp
The
.Fl n
option suppresses automatic printing.
.Fl e
adds a script expression and
.Fl f
reads one from a file.
.Pp
Extended regular expressions (`-E`), the hold space and the
.Ic n , Ns Ic N , Ns Ic D , Ns Ic P , Ns Ic G , Ns Ic H ,
.Ic h , Ns Ic x , Ns Ic b , Ns Ic t
and
.Ic \&:
commands are not implemented.
The target image currently requires file operands; standard input is a follow-up.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
0 on success, 2 for an invalid script or an I/O error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr grep 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD.
